*5b) Planned comparisons*
Last question: In another data set, I have 2 levels of condition A, and 3
levels of condition B. I would like to do two comparisons:
1) A1 vs A2 for B1 vs B2 and B3. In this case, I code A1 as 0.5 and A2 as
-0.5, and then B1 as 0.5 and B2 and B3 as -0.5.
2) A1 vs A2 for B2 vs B3. In this case, I am unsure: I thought of coding B2
as -0.5, B3 as 0.5, and B1 (the one I want to exclude from this comparison)
as 0.
Does this sound remotely right?
Or (for comparison 2), should I just fit a model on the B2 and B3 data?
(which I assume is not the best way to do this?)

Thanks very much again - I really appreciate the help, and being able to
bring these issues up to this forum.
