Hi Zhenguang,

You cannot compare the parameter estimates (either variance or correlation parameters) in the random-effects covariance matrices between models because the parameterizations are different.  Regarding correlations for the fixed effects estimates, the differences are small and probably due once again to the Laplace approximation of the likelihood and/or numerical precision issues.

Roger


