Hi Ariel,

The model comparisons in 1&2 are definitely not equivalent to those in 3&4, because word & root frequencies are serving as controls in each other's model comparisons in 1&2 but are absent in 3&4.  For example, including word frequency in the regression may soak up a considerable amount of otherwise unexplained variance and make the test in comparison 2 significant, whereas in comparison 4 there may be too much unexplained variance to reach significance for root frequency.

Best

Roger


